1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,388
Welcome to this technical walkthrough of AI-Based Predictive
Maintenance for Mining Equipment.

2
00:00:05,608 --> 00:00:14,014
The project team is Ganesh Mishra, Lakshya Sharma and Sagar
Patel, from Saskatchewan Polytechnic, under the guidance

3
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:15,826
of Doctor Himanshu Patel.

4
00:00:16,046 --> 00:00:23,479
This video explains the objectives, data sources, software
design, code and actual prediction outputs.

5
00:00:23,699 --> 00:00:29,218
The narration is computer generated; it is not a recording of
a team member speaking.

6
00:00:29,438 --> 00:00:35,871
The execution examples were run against the existing local
checkpoints and are replayed here for readability.

7
00:00:36,091 --> 00:00:40,509
The implemented task is current component fault
classification.

8
00:00:40,729 --> 00:00:47,637
Although predictive maintenance is the project title, the
software does not estimate the date of a future failure.

9
00:00:47,857 --> 00:00:51,791
That distinction will remain visible throughout the
demonstration.

10
00:00:52,011 --> 00:00:55,920
This chapter introduces the project team and their roles.

11
00:00:56,140 --> 00:00:59,433
Ganesh Mishra is the team lead and a developer.

12
00:00:59,653 --> 00:01:03,272
Lakshya Sharma is a developer and the team's tester.

13
00:01:03,492 --> 00:01:06,696
Sagar Patel is the planner and a developer.

14
00:01:06,916 --> 00:01:10,805
The project was supervised by Doctor Himanshu Patel.

15
00:01:11,025 --> 00:01:15,023
The same roles are listed in the final report and on the
poster.

16
00:01:15,243 --> 00:01:21,017
Mining operations depend on components such as bearings,
motors and geared drives.

17
00:01:21,237 --> 00:01:25,445
A fault in one component may interrupt the larger process.

18
00:01:25,665 --> 00:01:32,434
The project asks whether available condition-monitoring
measurements can support a practical fault-classification

19
00:01:32,434 --> 00:01:33,033
prototype.

20
00:01:33,253 --> 00:01:41,317
The software objective is straightforward: accept a supported
file, apply the correct preprocessing, load an existing

21
00:01:41,317 --> 00:01:44,280
model, and display its predicted condition.

22
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:51,114
The research objective is harder: compare sensor and visual
evidence using fault targets that are mechanically

23
00:01:51,114 --> 00:01:55,322
comparable, and test how results change under proper group
separation.

24
00:01:55,542 --> 00:02:00,871
A working upload button alone cannot establish that a
classifier generalizes.

25
00:02:01,091 --> 00:02:08,364
For that reason, the project keeps software execution checks
separate from held-out experimental performance.

26
00:02:08,584 --> 00:02:12,638
Both are necessary, but they answer different questions.

27
00:02:12,858 --> 00:02:18,496
The research background combines conventional condition
monitoring with visual transfer learning.

28
00:02:18,716 --> 00:02:26,390
Sensor measurements can be summarized using statistical and
spectral features, making tree ensembles, support vector

29
00:02:26,390 --> 00:02:29,763
machines and logistic regression useful candidates.

30
00:02:29,983 --> 00:02:35,087
Random forests provide a practical baseline for mixed
numerical features.

31
00:02:35,307 --> 00:02:41,715
For visual inputs, the project uses ImageNet-pretrained
ResNet18 representations.

32
00:02:41,935 --> 00:02:49,253
Most visual routes fine tune a classifier, while the gear-
tooth photograph route uses frozen features with logistic

33
00:02:49,253 --> 00:02:49,953
regression.

34
00:02:50,173 --> 00:02:54,277
These algorithm choices do not remove weaknesses in the data.

35
00:02:54,497 --> 00:03:01,445
A model may learn a recording, operating speed or camera setup
instead of a transferable fault signature.

36
00:03:01,665 --> 00:03:06,938
The central methodological choice is therefore the way
training and testing are separated.

37
00:03:07,158 --> 00:03:14,501
Dataset sources and model references are listed in the
references chapter near the end of this video, and in the
final

38
00:03:14,501 --> 00:03:14,936
report.

39
00:03:15,156 --> 00:03:24,056
The system contains eight mining-equipment application
mappings: Pump, Haul Truck, Belt Conveyor, Dozer, Excavator,

40
00:03:24,056 --> 00:03:27,229
Wheel Loader, Drill Rig and Motor Grader.

41
00:03:27,449 --> 00:03:32,177
These names describe intended applications of laboratory
components.

42
00:03:32,397 --> 00:03:37,301
They do not mean that every dataset was collected from the
named mining machine.

43
00:03:37,521 --> 00:03:40,945
Pump and Haul Truck use bearing-related evidence.

44
00:03:41,165 --> 00:03:47,013
Conveyor and Dozer use geared-drive evidence, with Dozer
reusing the conveyor benchmark.

45
00:03:47,233 --> 00:03:51,632
Excavator and Wheel Loader use related drive and motor tasks.

46
00:03:51,852 --> 00:03:58,335
Drill Rig uses gearbox data, while the aligned Motor Grader
comparison concerns gear damage.

47
00:03:58,555 --> 00:04:03,403
The original Motor Grader bearing route is also preserved as a
separate task.

48
00:04:03,623 --> 00:04:10,710
Reuse of the same rig or records is explicitly disclosed, so
eight application rows are not presented as eight

49
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:12,321
independent field trials.

50
00:04:12,541 --> 00:04:20,454
The sensor sources include Ottawa and UODS bearing
measurements, CORA electromechanical measurements, MCC5
gearbox

51
00:04:20,454 --> 00:04:25,313
vibration, Aalto gear measurements and the separate JUST
bearing task.

52
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:34,336
Visual sources include XJTU dynamic-vision recordings, CORA
infrared frames, synthetic MFGNet gear renders and real

53
00:04:34,336 --> 00:04:36,326
GearBox tooth photographs.

54
00:04:36,546 --> 00:04:40,524
Event-camera frames are not ordinary colour photographs.

55
00:04:40,744 --> 00:04:45,498
Synthetic renders are not camera measurements from damaged
mining equipment.

56
00:04:45,718 --> 00:04:53,170
Multiple frames, windows or tooth crops may come from one
source group, so their count must not be confused with a

57
00:04:53,170 --> 00:04:55,131
count of independent machines.

58
00:04:55,351 --> 00:05:00,429
The dataset manifest records the source mappings and available
local files.

59
00:05:00,649 --> 00:05:07,989
Raw data and large checkpoints stay outside the public code
archive, and the local installation needs access to those

60
00:05:07,989 --> 00:05:08,867
prerequisites.

61
00:05:09,087 --> 00:05:15,721
The block diagram begins with a file supplied through the
notebook, command line or local upload page.

62
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:20,979
The system validates the input and tries to identify a known
source format.

63
00:05:21,199 --> 00:05:28,305
If the source is compatible with more than one equipment
mapping, it returns an ambiguity warning rather than silently

64
00:05:28,305 --> 00:05:28,847
guessing.

65
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:33,830
A sensor file is converted into the features expected by its
checkpoint.

66
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:37,539
An image is transformed according to the visual route.

67
00:05:37,759 --> 00:05:44,537
The saved model produces class probabilities, and the largest
output determines the displayed condition.

68
00:05:44,757 --> 00:05:50,776
Both modalities share the same prediction entry point, but
they remain independent models.

69
00:05:50,996 --> 00:05:54,994
There is no fusion of unrelated sensor and image samples.

70
00:05:55,214 --> 00:06:02,418
The final output includes the application mapping, fault
label, model probability and model used.

71
00:06:02,638 --> 00:06:07,476
The submitted notebook is the main explanation and
demonstration entry point.

72
00:06:07,696 --> 00:06:15,439
Its first code cell imports the standard libraries, numerical
packages, plotting tools and upload widgets.

73
00:06:15,659 --> 00:06:21,308
It locates the project folder and imports predictive
maintenance as the application module.

74
00:06:21,528 --> 00:06:28,533
The implementation is kept in that companion Python file so
the notebook does not duplicate thousands of lines of

75
00:06:28,533 --> 00:06:30,145
model and interface logic.

76
00:06:30,365 --> 00:06:34,169
The notebook and companion code must be submitted together.

77
00:06:34,389 --> 00:06:41,609
Selecting the correct environment is important because the
application depends on packages for numerical processing,

78
00:06:41,609 --> 00:06:43,476
images and checkpoint loading.

79
00:06:43,696 --> 00:06:47,580
Running the inference demonstration should not start training.

80
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:54,866
The existing checkpoints are reused, and missing local assets
are reported explicitly rather than replaced by

81
00:06:54,866 --> 00:06:56,162
fabricated examples.

82
00:06:56,382 --> 00:07:01,431
Before showing predictions, the notebook displays the
checkpoint status.

83
00:07:01,651 --> 00:07:08,521
The application has eight main sensor routes and eight main
image routes, plus the additional Aalto gear sensor route

84
00:07:08,521 --> 00:07:09,519
for Motor Grader.

85
00:07:09,739 --> 00:07:16,615
A checkpoint can be present on disk without being trusted, and
a trusted filename alone does not prove that a real

86
00:07:16,615 --> 00:07:17,882
prediction will work.

87
00:07:18,102 --> 00:07:21,631
The status table is therefore only the first check.

88
00:07:21,851 --> 00:07:25,060
It is followed by actual inference calls.

89
00:07:25,280 --> 00:07:30,673
The local verification found all required checkpoint files and
their registrations.

90
00:07:30,893 --> 00:07:35,292
The saved models remain unchanged during this video
preparation.

91
00:07:35,512 --> 00:07:42,490
The code archive deliberately excludes their large binaries,
so someone running a fresh copy needs the documented

92
00:07:42,490 --> 00:07:45,454
local assets as well as the Python dependencies.

93
00:07:45,674 --> 00:07:52,757
The sensor loading code examines known file structures rather
than accepting every numerical table as interchangeable.

94
00:07:52,977 --> 00:08:02,435
Supported CSV schemas identify expected channel names for
Ottawa, UODS, MCC5, JUST and Aalto sources.

95
00:08:02,655 --> 00:08:07,378
Original MAT recordings are also supported for relevant
bearing sources.

96
00:08:07,598 --> 00:08:12,327
CORA recordings have a source-specific naming and acquisition
convention.

97
00:08:12,547 --> 00:08:18,945
These checks matter because sampling rates, channel meanings
and units affect the extracted features.

98
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:25,783
A pressure column cannot be substituted for an acceleration
channel merely because both contain numbers.

99
00:08:26,003 --> 00:08:32,916
The application rejects an unrecognized CSV schema instead of
passing incompatible values into a model.

100
00:08:33,136 --> 00:08:40,108
Source recognition is not a universal machine-identification
algorithm; it identifies compatibility with the

101
00:08:40,108 --> 00:08:43,788
laboratory pipelines already implemented in this project.

102
00:08:44,008 --> 00:08:50,693
Cleaning in this project means validating the measurements and
applying the source-specific preparation expected by a

103
00:08:50,693 --> 00:08:51,036
model.

104
00:08:51,256 --> 00:08:57,139
Readers check numeric values and whether enough samples are
available for a complete feature window.

105
00:08:57,359 --> 00:09:02,968
Later checks reject nonfinite features and feature sets that
do not match the checkpoint.

106
00:09:03,188 --> 00:09:08,006
These controls prevent a model from receiving the wrong
columns in the wrong order.

107
00:09:08,226 --> 00:09:15,648
Sensor features include quantities such as root mean square,
standard deviation, crest factor and selected

108
00:09:15,648 --> 00:09:17,539
frequency-domain summaries.

109
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:22,742
Some sources use shaft-order information when rotational speed
is available.

110
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:27,896
Preprocessing is not simply deleting missing rows and hoping
for a good score.

111
00:09:28,116 --> 00:09:34,723
Its purpose is to preserve a consistent relationship between
the original measurement, the extracted features and the

112
00:09:34,723 --> 00:09:36,473
model that was trained on them.

113
00:09:36,693 --> 00:09:41,297
Root mean square is the square root of the average squared
signal amplitude.

114
00:09:41,517 --> 00:09:47,235
It summarizes signal energy but does not independently
identify a particular fault.

115
00:09:47,455 --> 00:09:54,028
Crest factor compares a peak amplitude with the root mean
square value and can describe impulsive behaviour.

116
00:09:54,248 --> 00:09:59,177
Spectral features summarize the distribution of energy across
frequency.

117
00:09:59,397 --> 00:10:05,725
In sources where speed is known, shaft-order features express
frequency relative to rotation.

118
00:10:05,945 --> 00:10:12,509
These measurements can change with operating conditions as
well as damage, which explains why speed and load

119
00:10:12,509 --> 00:10:14,028
separation are important.

120
00:10:14,248 --> 00:10:18,532
The model learns combinations of features from labelled
examples.

121
00:10:18,752 --> 00:10:22,890
A large feature value is not automatically a failure warning.

122
00:10:23,110 --> 00:10:30,226
At inference, the selected checkpoint determines exactly which
feature columns are required and which preprocessing

123
00:10:30,226 --> 00:10:31,773
pipeline must be applied.

124
00:10:31,993 --> 00:10:37,036
The main evaluation safeguards are visible in the notebook
split demonstration.

125
00:10:37,256 --> 00:10:41,685
Complete recordings or operating groups are assigned to the
test side.

126
00:10:41,905 --> 00:10:46,583
Individual windows from a held-out recording cannot be placed
in training.

127
00:10:46,803 --> 00:10:52,087
Pump uses separate speed profiles or operating speeds for its
two datasets.

128
00:10:52,307 --> 00:10:55,246
CORA holds out whole speed settings.

129
00:10:55,466 --> 00:11:00,020
Haul Truck sensor evaluation uses held-out bearing identities.

130
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:07,383
The aligned Motor Grader sensor experiment leaves gear pairs
out, while its photo task uses source groups.

131
00:11:07,603 --> 00:11:13,461
These protocols are not identical, and their differences
remain part of the interpretation.

132
00:11:13,681 --> 00:11:18,414
Inner validation selects models or training settings within
the training data.

133
00:11:18,634 --> 00:11:25,799
This reduces direct leakage from the final evaluation group,
although dataset confounding and limited independent

134
00:11:25,799 --> 00:11:29,097
specimens can still restrict scientific conclusions.

135
00:11:29,317 --> 00:11:36,534
The sensor code defines several candidate classifiers rather
than forcing a single algorithm onto every dataset.

136
00:11:36,754 --> 00:11:44,915
The candidate family includes random forest, extra trees,
histogram gradient boosting, a radial-basis support vector

137
00:11:44,915 --> 00:11:47,167
machine and logistic regression.

138
00:11:47,387 --> 00:11:54,435
Scaling is contained inside the relevant estimator pipeline,
so its parameters are fitted with training data.

139
00:11:54,655 --> 00:11:57,489
Class weighting is used where configured.

140
00:11:57,709 --> 00:12:03,587
The chosen candidate can differ across evaluation folds and
across application mappings.

141
00:12:03,807 --> 00:12:10,115
The notebook displays these settings by instantiating the
candidate factories and reading their parameters.

142
00:12:10,335 --> 00:12:15,134
Deployment uses the saved final estimator and its selected
feature list.

143
00:12:15,354 --> 00:12:20,257
It does not repeat candidate selection each time a user
uploads a file.

144
00:12:20,477 --> 00:12:26,835
This keeps inference reproducible and avoids confusing
prediction latency with a new training experiment.

145
00:12:27,055 --> 00:12:34,003
The visual route reads a supported image, applies its
configured transforms and uses a saved model to obtain

146
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:34,903
probabilities.

147
00:12:35,123 --> 00:12:39,582
Seven main image routes use ResNet18-based classifiers.

148
00:12:39,802 --> 00:12:48,045
Motor Grader tooth photographs follow a separate path: frozen
ResNet18 features feed a logistic-regression classifier.

149
00:12:48,265 --> 00:12:52,943
This distinction is important when explaining which model
produced an answer.

150
00:12:53,163 --> 00:12:58,397
Inference runs without gradient calculation and with the model
in evaluation mode.

151
00:12:58,617 --> 00:13:03,465
The system is not trained to diagnose arbitrary whole-machine
photographs.

152
00:13:03,685 --> 00:13:11,283
Supported event frames, thermal frames, synthetic gear renders
and tooth crops have different visual meanings and

153
00:13:11,283 --> 00:13:12,023
provenance.

154
00:13:12,243 --> 00:13:18,376
A photo of an entire grader does not provide the same evidence
as a labelled tooth inspection crop.

155
00:13:18,596 --> 00:13:22,870
Unknown image sources must remain unsupported or ambiguous.

156
00:13:23,090 --> 00:13:29,428
Data augmentation is applied only to training images, never to
validation or test images.

157
00:13:29,648 --> 00:13:36,524
It imitates nuisance variation that should not change the
fault label, and a seeded random generator keeps runs

158
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,206
repeatable.

159
00:13:37,426 --> 00:13:44,868
Event-camera and infrared frames receive random horizontal
flips, shifts of up to eight pixels, brightness scaling

160
00:13:44,868 --> 00:13:49,373
between zero point eight and one point two, and small Gaussian
noise.

161
00:13:49,593 --> 00:13:56,766
Rendered gears are rotated by multiples of ninety degrees,
mirrored and shifted by up to six pixels, because a gear

162
00:13:56,766 --> 00:13:59,636
looks the same when it is turned or reflected.

163
00:13:59,856 --> 00:14:04,329
The gear-tooth photo route uses frozen features and is not
augmented.

164
00:14:04,549 --> 00:14:12,114
Sensor recordings are not augmented either; each recording
already gives many windows, and class weighting handles

165
00:14:12,114 --> 00:14:12,777
imbalance.

166
00:14:12,997 --> 00:14:20,721
Across the thirty-five outer evaluation rounds, inner
validation selected logistic regression thirteen times and
extra

167
00:14:20,721 --> 00:14:21,965
trees twelve times.

168
00:14:22,185 --> 00:14:29,808
Gradient boosting was chosen five times, random forest three
times and the RBF support vector machine twice.

169
00:14:30,028 --> 00:14:36,011
No single classifier won every mapping, which is why the full
candidate set is kept.

170
00:14:36,231 --> 00:14:42,770
The central prediction function is the connection between the
notebook, command line and local upload page.

171
00:14:42,990 --> 00:14:48,373
It first handles the special tooth-image route when Motor
Grader is explicitly selected.

172
00:14:48,593 --> 00:14:52,267
Other inputs are passed through source identification.

173
00:14:52,487 --> 00:14:58,250
If a user selects a mapping incompatible with that source, the
function raises an error.

174
00:14:58,470 --> 00:15:05,546
If the source matches several candidates and no reliable
choice has been made, it returns an ambiguous equipment

175
00:15:05,546 --> 00:15:05,988
result.

176
00:15:06,208 --> 00:15:13,391
Otherwise it scores the appropriate checkpoint, selects the
most probable class and assembles the answer fields.

177
00:15:13,611 --> 00:15:20,219
The common entry point reduces the risk that different
interfaces accidentally apply different preprocessing.

178
00:15:20,439 --> 00:15:28,059
It also keeps source identification separate from fault
classification, which is essential for equipment mappings that

179
00:15:28,059 --> 00:15:29,932
share one laboratory dataset.

180
00:15:30,152 --> 00:15:36,665
The notebook upload interface uses a file-upload widget, a
mapping dropdown and a prediction button.

181
00:15:36,885 --> 00:15:44,292
The upload accepts supported sensor recordings or image
formats, but format acceptance does not guarantee source

182
00:15:44,292 --> 00:15:45,218
compatibility.

183
00:15:45,438 --> 00:15:49,601
The callback first checks whether a file was actually
supplied.

184
00:15:49,821 --> 00:15:54,895
It then passes the temporary input to the same application
prediction function.

185
00:15:55,115 --> 00:15:59,378
Automatic routing is useful only where the source can be
established.

186
00:15:59,598 --> 00:16:06,156
The dropdown remains necessary for shared laboratory formats
and the explicit gear-tooth inspection route.

187
00:16:06,376 --> 00:16:12,983
The interface should display either a condition prediction
with its model information or a clear explanation of why

188
00:16:12,983 --> 00:16:14,534
the input cannot be scored.

189
00:16:14,754 --> 00:16:22,321
A user confirmation selects an application mapping; it does
not turn laboratory data into real measurements from that

190
00:16:22,321 --> 00:16:23,291
mining machine.

191
00:16:23,511 --> 00:16:29,870
This panel shows the actual output of a Pump sensor inference
call using an available local recording.

192
00:16:30,090 --> 00:16:37,458
The application identifies a compatible bearing source,
extracts the expected features and loads the trusted sensor

193
00:16:37,458 --> 00:16:38,162
checkpoint.

194
00:16:38,382 --> 00:16:42,706
The predicted class and probability are returned with the
model name.

195
00:16:42,926 --> 00:16:48,434
The example is useful for demonstrating that the complete path
works from file to answer.

196
00:16:48,654 --> 00:16:53,028
It must not be described as a fresh held-out accuracy
measurement.

197
00:16:53,248 --> 00:16:59,911
The route-check samples can be fitting data, and the archived
evaluation uses its own group separation.

198
00:17:00,131 --> 00:17:05,925
The application mapping is Pump, while the source remains an
Ottawa bearing-rig measurement.

199
00:17:06,145 --> 00:17:12,578
That distinction keeps the demonstration truthful without
reducing the value of showing a real model execute

200
00:17:12,578 --> 00:17:13,352
successfully.

201
00:17:13,572 --> 00:17:18,536
The Pump image example uses a local event-camera frame with
known provenance.

202
00:17:18,756 --> 00:17:23,964
The model returns its current-condition classification and
class probabilities.

203
00:17:24,184 --> 00:17:31,810
An event frame represents changes observed by a dynamic-vision
sensor; it is different from a standard RGB photograph

204
00:17:31,810 --> 00:17:32,462
of a pump.

205
00:17:32,682 --> 00:17:39,987
Its supported size and channel pattern help identify the
source family, while local source indexing can establish a

206
00:17:39,987 --> 00:17:40,940
unique mapping.

207
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:47,773
The sensor and image examples are separate observations, not
synchronized recordings of one machine.

208
00:17:47,993 --> 00:17:52,772
Showing them beside each other demonstrates two independent
prediction routes.

209
00:17:52,992 --> 00:18:00,744
It does not demonstrate fusion, causal superiority of one
modality, or the ability to detect an internal bearing fault

210
00:18:00,744 --> 00:18:02,649
from an arbitrary photograph.

211
00:18:02,869 --> 00:18:06,948
Those stronger claims would require additional matched
evidence.

212
00:18:07,168 --> 00:18:12,611
Motor Grader needs special explanation because two component
tasks are retained.

213
00:18:12,831 --> 00:18:17,085
The original sensor route diagnoses slewing-bearing
conditions.

214
00:18:17,305 --> 00:18:23,723
The aligned comparison adds an Aalto gear sensor checkpoint
for a broad healthy-versus-damaged gear target.

215
00:18:23,943 --> 00:18:31,031
Here the actual local Aalto recording produces a healthy
prediction with a probability of zero point nine eight seven.

216
00:18:31,251 --> 00:18:34,670
This is a deployment response on a fitting recording.

217
00:18:34,890 --> 00:18:39,143
It is not ninety-eight point seven percent held-out accuracy.

218
00:18:39,363 --> 00:18:44,447
The independent gear-pair experiment is the evidence used to
discuss generalization.

219
00:18:44,667 --> 00:18:51,200
The Aalto dataset is a laboratory gearbox analogue, not a
field recording from a Motor Grader.

220
00:18:51,420 --> 00:18:57,695
Preserving both routes avoids deleting working evidence while
making the component comparison more mechanically

221
00:18:57,695 --> 00:18:58,317
defensible.

222
00:18:58,537 --> 00:19:05,105
The Motor Grader image route scores a real tooth inspection
crop using the saved feature-based classifier.

223
00:19:05,325 --> 00:19:11,863
The example panel shows the actual damaged-tooth prediction
and the fields returned by that implementation.

224
00:19:12,083 --> 00:19:18,587
The model confidence display is still an uncalibrated output
and should not be interpreted as certainty of real

225
00:19:18,587 --> 00:19:19,641
equipment failure.

226
00:19:19,861 --> 00:19:27,015
Sensor and image tasks share a broad gear-condition target,
but one label is attached to a gear-pair run and the other

227
00:19:27,015 --> 00:19:28,349
to a local tooth crop.

228
00:19:28,569 --> 00:19:31,078
Their physical gears are different.

229
00:19:31,298 --> 00:19:38,469
The existing tests therefore support a comparison of related
classification tasks, not a paired same-grader

230
00:19:38,469 --> 00:19:39,206
experiment.

231
00:19:39,426 --> 00:19:45,968
The original bearing checkpoint remains available
independently and should not be substituted into this gear-
tooth

232
00:19:45,968 --> 00:19:46,599
comparison.

233
00:19:46,819 --> 00:19:52,392
This execution supplies a compatible CORA recording without
selecting an equipment mapping.

234
00:19:52,612 --> 00:19:58,425
The expected behaviour is an ambiguous equipment response
listing the supported candidates.

235
00:19:58,645 --> 00:20:05,453
The system cannot infer that an identical laboratory source
must belong to one particular whole mining machine.

236
00:20:05,673 --> 00:20:12,136
This is a reliability feature, not a missing classification
trick that should be bypassed with a guess.

237
00:20:12,356 --> 00:20:19,197
Manual mapping confirmation allows a known task to be
evaluated, but it does not create new evidence about the

238
00:20:19,197 --> 00:20:20,814
original physical machine.

239
00:20:21,034 --> 00:20:24,347
The same principle applies to image provenance.

240
00:20:24,567 --> 00:20:30,775
A visually similar frame can remain ambiguous when its source
index cannot establish a unique route.

241
00:20:30,995 --> 00:20:37,532
The final demonstration should explain this behaviour clearly
rather than presenting every upload as automatic

242
00:20:37,532 --> 00:20:38,423
identification.

243
00:20:38,643 --> 00:20:45,796
The invalid-input examples test ordinary text, an unrecognized
CSV and corrupted image bytes.

244
00:20:46,016 --> 00:20:53,264
Each example was actually sent to the prediction function, and
the displayed response records the resulting rejection.

245
00:20:53,484 --> 00:20:59,732
These checks matter because an upload control can accept a
filename even when the content is unusable.

246
00:20:59,952 --> 00:21:05,051
The model-loading path also verifies checkpoint trust and
expected metadata.

247
00:21:05,271 --> 00:21:11,774
A missing or untrusted checkpoint must not be replaced with a
random estimator or a fabricated prediction.

248
00:21:11,994 --> 00:21:18,357
Errors should explain why the input could not be scored, while
leaving the working application stable.

249
00:21:18,577 --> 00:21:25,946
These examples demonstrate handling of specific tested cases;
they are not a guarantee that every imaginable malformed

250
00:21:25,946 --> 00:21:27,444
file has been exhausted.

251
00:21:27,664 --> 00:21:34,551
The complete route check executed thirty-nine saved-model
examples successfully, covering all eight sensor and image

252
00:21:34,551 --> 00:21:37,282
mappings plus the additional Aalto gear route.

253
00:21:37,502 --> 00:21:42,611
Unsupported-file rejection and shared-CORA ambiguity checks
also passed.

254
00:21:42,831 --> 00:21:50,501
The important qualification is the definition of pass: a model
loaded, accepted a compatible input and returned the

255
00:21:50,501 --> 00:21:51,568
required output.

256
00:21:51,788 --> 00:21:57,871
Two Drill Rig images were classified as healthy when their
source labels were gear wear and gear pitting.

257
00:21:58,091 --> 00:22:03,185
Those cases remain visible as prediction errors even though
execution succeeded.

258
00:22:03,405 --> 00:22:10,631
The clean publication checkout passed two hundred fifty-five
automated tests, with two tests skipped because local

259
00:22:10,631 --> 00:22:12,153
data were not available.

260
00:22:12,373 --> 00:22:19,475
These counts come from earlier verification runs; the test
suite was not rerun while this video was prepared.

261
00:22:19,695 --> 00:22:24,124
The final report contains the independent experimental
results.

262
00:22:24,344 --> 00:22:31,042
Pump reached ninety-five point eight three percent sensor
balanced accuracy and one hundred percent visual balanced

263
00:22:31,042 --> 00:22:34,071
accuracy under their respective recording protocols.

264
00:22:34,291 --> 00:22:40,789
Those protocols and rigs differ, so the result does not
establish that vision is universally better.

265
00:22:41,009 --> 00:22:45,103
The CORA tasks showed weak transfer to unseen speeds.

266
00:22:45,323 --> 00:22:50,497
Haul Truck had weaker visual recognition and a load-confounded
ball-fault class.

267
00:22:50,717 --> 00:22:57,665
Motor Grader's aligned gear sensor result was seventy-seven
point seven eight percent balanced accuracy, while the

268
00:22:57,665 --> 00:23:01,200
tooth-photo result was eighty-two point five nine percent.

269
00:23:01,420 --> 00:23:08,083
Its high raw photo accuracy is affected by class imbalance,
and damaged-tooth recall is lower.

270
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:15,151
The poster shows these same held-out balanced accuracies, and
the report gives the full numerical evidence.

271
00:23:15,371 --> 00:23:22,591
Supplementary time-split checks use the first sixty percent of
a recording for training, discard a ten percent gap and

272
00:23:22,591 --> 00:23:24,548
test on the last thirty percent.

273
00:23:24,768 --> 00:23:29,187
Several saved results are much higher than the unseen-speed
results.

274
00:23:29,407 --> 00:23:33,406
This is not a reason to hide the more difficult evaluations.

275
00:23:33,626 --> 00:23:36,944
The two protocols ask different questions.

276
00:23:37,164 --> 00:23:44,148
A later segment of a known recording can retain the same
speed, specimen and acquisition signature as training.

277
00:23:44,368 --> 00:23:51,111
A gap reduces direct temporal overlap, but it does not create
a new machine or operating condition.

278
00:23:51,331 --> 00:23:57,154
The report labels these scores separately and notes that
fitting settings and sample pools can differ.

279
00:23:57,374 --> 00:24:04,541
No score from this procedure establishes future failure
forecasting, and no unsupported time-split result is assigned

280
00:24:04,541 --> 00:24:06,991
to a mapping without a saved experiment.

281
00:24:07,211 --> 00:24:14,454
The practical outcome is a working educational prototype for
component inspection and reproducible model comparison.

282
00:24:14,674 --> 00:24:22,862
It demonstrates data ingestion, feature preparation, trusted
model reuse, ambiguity handling and prediction output

283
00:24:22,862 --> 00:24:24,802
through a common interface.

284
00:24:25,022 --> 00:24:29,375
Its remaining limitations are scientific as well as
operational.

285
00:24:29,595 --> 00:24:37,696
Some datasets share records, image crops remain related,
synthetic renders need validation against real photographs,

286
00:24:37,696 --> 00:24:41,537
and confidence values are not calibrated failure risks.

287
00:24:41,757 --> 00:24:47,176
The code package also needs local data and checkpoints to run
the full demonstration.

288
00:24:47,396 --> 00:24:54,425
Before a real maintenance decision could rely on this system,
additional work would need site-specific measurements,

289
00:24:54,425 --> 00:25:00,302
balanced operating conditions, independent machines and a
clear assessment of missed-fault costs.

290
00:25:00,522 --> 00:25:07,775
The present software should support investigation and
explanation, not replace qualified engineering judgment.

291
00:25:07,995 --> 00:25:11,799
This chapter lists the main sources used in the project.

292
00:25:12,019 --> 00:25:20,456
The sensor data come from the Ottawa and UODS bearing
datasets, the CORA electromechanical dataset, the MCC5-THU

293
00:25:20,456 --> 00:25:26,105
gearbox data, the Aalto gear failure dataset and a slewing-
bearing dataset.

294
00:25:26,325 --> 00:25:35,104
The image data come from the XJTU dynamic-vision dataset, CORA
infrared frames, MFGNet gear renders and the GearBox

295
00:25:35,104 --> 00:25:36,478
tooth photographs.

296
00:25:36,698 --> 00:25:43,091
All nine public datasets are published under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 licence.

297
00:25:43,311 --> 00:25:49,125
The models build on Breiman's random forests and on the
residual networks of He and colleagues.

298
00:25:49,345 --> 00:25:56,206
The mining context and the evaluation design draw on Dayo-
Olupona and colleagues' review of predictive maintenance in

299
00:25:56,206 --> 00:26:02,012
mining, Zhao and colleagues' diagnosis benchmark, and Kaufman
and colleagues' work on data leakage.

300
00:26:02,232 --> 00:26:06,970
The final report lists all twenty-four references with full
citations.

301
00:26:07,190 --> 00:26:14,343
To conclude, the coding phase provides one integrated notebook
backed by a reusable Python implementation.

302
00:26:14,563 --> 00:26:21,904
It accepts supported sensor recordings or component images,
checks source compatibility, loads an existing model and

303
00:26:21,904 --> 00:26:25,765
returns a fault label with model information and probability.

304
00:26:25,985 --> 00:26:32,868
Where source evidence cannot distinguish equipment mappings,
the system reports ambiguity rather than guessing.

305
00:26:33,088 --> 00:26:40,219
Real local execution checks confirm that the supported routes
run, including the aligned Aalto gear sensor and Motor

306
00:26:40,219 --> 00:26:41,756
Grader tooth-image paths.

307
00:26:41,976 --> 00:26:49,669
The final report explains the actual held-out results, the
supplementary time-split check and the unsuccessful cases.

308
00:26:49,889 --> 00:26:55,632
The project is complete as a laboratory-based demonstration
with scientific limitations.

309
00:26:55,852 --> 00:27:02,863
Future work should improve independent data and validation
before expanding claims about mining-field reliability or

310
00:27:02,863 --> 00:27:04,435
future failure prediction.

311
00:27:04,655 --> 00:27:06,684
Thank you for watching.
